WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.290
Every Microsoft agreement starts

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:03.960
with a set of choices.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.460
For a university, the value comes

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.960
from making those choices clearly

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.960
and having the right support around them.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.290
Data#3 brings more than thirty years

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.290
of education experience,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.960
long-standing engagement

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:17.960
with CAUDIT members,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.020
and national coverage across Australia,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.100
Fiji and the Pacific.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.420
Each institution has a

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.030
local account contact,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.000
backed by Microsoft licensing

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.960
and contract specialists,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.770
national solution experts,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.730
and direct escalation pathways

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.960
into Microsoft.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.700
That team supports the

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.960
full agreement lifecycle.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.010
It coordinates quotes, orders, enrolments,

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.960
amendments and renewals.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.960
It interprets licensing requirements,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.100
provides education-specific guidance,

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.280
reviews consumption and

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.540
licensing positions,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.960
models renewal scenarios,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.850
and advocates for customers

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.960
when licensing, entitlement

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.960
or operational issues need escalation.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.960
The level of support remains flexible.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.700
Institutions with strong

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.010
internal capability

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.780
can focus on core licensing administration

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.100
and enquiries.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.340
Those wanting deeper

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.030
support can add reviews,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.100
planning, roadmap briefings, governance

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.030
and specialist engagement

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.960
as priorities change.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.850
MyD3 provides a secure central view

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.960
of agreements, software

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.150
and cloud reporting,

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.990
quotes, orders, assets, support cases

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.100
and lifecycle information.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.010
Optional Premier Support adds accountable

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.950
incident ownership across Microsoft cloud

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.030
and on-premises technology,

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:40.960
using a pre-purchased pool of hours

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.690
and escalation to Microsoft

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.960
when product intervention is required.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.860
Around Azure, separately scoped services

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.960
can provide platform support,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.210
priority incident

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.170
handling, cost visibility,

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.970
right-sizing, governance, monitoring

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.100
and managed operations.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.260
The same relationship

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.860
can connect institutions

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.310
with expertise across

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.960
modern work, security,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.960
data and artificial intelligence,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.960
applications and automation.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.410
Engagement can take

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.210
the form of consulting,

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.540
packaged services, projects

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.960
or ongoing managed services.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.110
Each is scoped and purchased separately

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.100
from the Microsoft agreement.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.100
University priorities change over time.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.520
Licensing optimisation may lead

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.030
to cloud adoption, security uplift,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.410
responsible artificial

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.970
intelligence adoption

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.960
or broader transformation.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.860
Data#3 helps bring the right expertise

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.100
into the relationship at the right time.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.990
The next agreement cycle begins

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.560
by confirming scope and requirements,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.220
validating licensing and

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.030
enrolment information,

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.990
completing documentation,

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.960
preparing onboarding and handover,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.700
then verifying licences

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.100
and beginning ongoing support.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.652
Your Microsoft investment.

00:02:58.963 --> 00:02:59.861
Your way.

00:03:00.343 --> 00:03:01.969
Backed by Data#3.
